cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Detectability, please cite it as below."
title: "Detectability: Pre-survey detectability, modelled and reproducible"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Detectability predicts, before fieldwork, whether a gravity or magnetic survey will detect a buried target. It
  models the anomaly of simple near-surface targets (sphere, horizontal and vertical cylinder, rectangular prism,
  dipping dyke, vertical contact) along a profile, takes the main geomagnetic field from IGRF-14 for the survey
  location and date, compares the anomaly with instrument and field noise, and returns a verdict per method with the
  recommended station spacing, profile length, assumptions and a script that reproduces the result. Every model is
  validated against an independent result, including an independent code (Harmonica).
